# The Quota slice: the witness, years later (design/spine-plan/02-WITNESS.md; engine: world/witness.mjs; check:
# tools/witnesscheck.mjs). Anni Haldane at forty, at her own table, telling her daughter what she saw of that
# winter, with the player's own man sitting there old. She tells only what she saw or was told (reach, sources,
# never). The ledger the read-back used to print (q_readback.lwd, @readback q.record) is the oracle underneath:
# every row it would print is answered by a beat here or declared unwitnessed. No beat is skipped, nothing sums
# him up, and it ends on an effect. Game director, 2026-10-22.

@witness q.w.anni
who: ANNI
listener: DAUGHTER
guest: q_class inspector=NED militia=WILL
place: q_anni_room
opens: q.w.anni.open
dispatch: q.w.anni.next
reach: q_haldane, q_post, q_road_home, q_granary, q_tilney, q_yard, q_furrowe_door, q_furrowe_kitchen, q_anni_room
sources: BET, ILO, AARON, EDIE, STORE, WALTER
never: q_returns, q_cells, q_office, q_brack_kitchen
beat: q.w.anni.paper | q_figure, q.true_in_hand | seen q_haldane ? true
beat: q.w.anni.post | q_cart, q_class, said.ned_sign_cart, said.ned_vouch_cart, q.cart_counted, said.will_take_four, said.will_take_six, said.will_let_through, said.will_refuse_holt, said.will_arrest_tomas, said.ned_free_tomas, q.cart_stripped | seen q_post ? q_cart != none
beat: q.w.anni.mary | q.ned_looked | seen q_post ? q_class == inspector
beat: q.w.anni.store | said.ned_report_true, said.ned_report_inflated, said.ned_report_blamed, said.will_report_true, said.will_report_inflated, said.will_report_blamed | heard STORE ? q_figure != none
beat: q.w.anni.granary | q_door, q.will_down, q.read_aloud, said.read_true_door | seen q_granary ? q_door != none
beat: q.w.anni.week | q.tomas_held, q.ilo_mark, q.dorrah_taken | heard ILO ? has(q.tomas_held)
beat: q.w.anni.yard | q.aaron_taken, said.ned_vouch_yard, said.will_next_door, said.will_takes_aaron | seen q_yard ? seen(q.fate.yard)
beat: q.w.anni.gate | q.anni_sent, q.anni_furrowe, q.ned_claimed, q.ned_parentage, q.ned_food, q.will_bread | seen q_tilney ? seen(q.fate.gate)
beat: q.w.anni.table | haldane, bowls, food, portion, furrowe, brack, taken | seen q_haldane ? true
beat: q.w.anni.hands | said.will_leave_thread | heard EDIE ? q_class == militia
beat: q.w.anni.guest | said.ned_keep_tally, q.corner_known, q.pencil_kept, q.pencil_rubbed | seen q_anni_room ? true
last: q.w.anni.tin
unwitnessed: q.log_two, q.log_true | Tesk's oats by the cell door: she never saw the cells, and nobody who did ever told her about the oats
unwitnessed: q.pencil_kept, q.pencil_rubbed | the wedge under the scale at first light: she was never on the square that early, and Walter Mott never told
oracle: q.record

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the opening: the tin
@node q.w.anni.open
place: q_anni_room
speaker: ANNI
cost: 3
camera: near
nar: Anni's kitchen, years later. The same oilcloth. The tin on the table with the lid off and the knotted lengths of wool out in a row. Anni is forty, and her daughter is twelve, and it's raining, the fine kind that soaks you.
line: DAUGHTER: What's all these?
line: ANNI: Knots. Put them back the way they were, they go in order.
line: DAUGHTER: Of what, though?
line: ANNI: That one's sacks. That's lamps, Exchange Street, all the way down.
line: ANNI: That one's stairs. {when: has(q.anni_sent)}
line: DAUGHTER: Whose stairs? {when: has(q.anni_sent)}
line: ANNI: The home on Tilney Road. I counted them going in. {when: has(q.anni_sent)}
line: DAUGHTER: Why?
line: ANNI: So I'd know how far it was back down.
nar: A knock at the door. An old man from the allocation office, come about the back room, because somebody has to come about the back room. He has his hat in his hand, and there's a pale mark on the front of it where a badge used to be. {when: q_class == inspector, sense: door.knock}
nar: A knock at the door. An old man with a parcel of mending in brown paper, which Edie Brack has finished for her, because Edie can't get up the hill now and somebody has to bring it. He stands there with his cap in his hand. {when: q_class == militia}
nar: Anni lets him in out of the rain and gives him tea in the good cup, and he sits at the end of the table, and she goes on with her daughter as if he were the coal man.
voice: dark: You know this table. You know the hinge marks. {dc: 2}
go: q.w.anni.next

@node q.w.anni.next
cost: 0
alt: e3.start ? seen(q.w.anni.tin)
do: wnext()
alt: q.w.anni.paper ? wat(q.w.anni.paper)
alt: q.w.anni.post ? wat(q.w.anni.post)
alt: q.w.anni.mary ? wat(q.w.anni.mary)
alt: q.w.anni.store ? wat(q.w.anni.store)
alt: q.w.anni.granary ? wat(q.w.anni.granary)
alt: q.w.anni.week ? wat(q.w.anni.week)
alt: q.w.anni.yard ? wat(q.w.anni.yard)
alt: q.w.anni.gate ? wat(q.w.anni.gate)
alt: q.w.anni.table ? wat(q.w.anni.table)
alt: q.w.anni.hands ? wat(q.w.anni.hands)
alt: q.w.anni.guest ? wat(q.w.anni.guest)
go: q.w.anni.tin

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the beats
@node q.w.anni.paper
place: q_anni_room
speaker: ANNI
cost: 3
line: ANNI: They came on the Monday with the brigade. A man stood in our yard in a good coat and said we owed them sacks. He said it like it was weather.
voice: sum: The arm went down. You stood there and watched it go down. Nobody can say you didn't. {echo: q.sl.signed, when: toldself(q.sl.signed)}
line: ANNI: Your uncle Tomas took my knots into town. He didn't tell Mum. He thought if somebody came and looked, they'd see.
go: q.w.anni.next

@node q.w.anni.post
place: q_anni_room
speaker: ANNI
cost: 4
line: ANNI: We took the cart to the post with what was left. Six sacks. I counted them off out loud while the constable put his bayonet in them. {count: cost}
voice: ballast: If one cart goes through, forty go tomorrow, and then there's no post. There's just you on a road. {echo: q.sl.forty_carts, when: toldself(q.sl.forty_carts)}
line: ANNI: The sergeant had his hands in his armpits the whole time. {when: q_class == militia}
line: ANNI: He stood by the fire in his good coat and kept saying only. It's only four, Mrs Haldane. It's only till the review. {when: has(said.ned_sign_cart)}
line: ANNI: He climbed up in his good coat and lifted every one down himself, and said my numbers back to me. Then he carried the four to the hut anyway. {when: has(q.cart_counted)}
line: ANNI: He said Furrowe, with an e on the end. Like he was spelling it for somebody. Mum laughed about that after. Not then. {when: has(said.ned_vouch_cart)}
line: ANNI: The sergeant put the sacks back. Slow, so we could watch him do it. Tomas did his voice all the way to Osby. {when: has(said.will_let_through)}
line: ANNI: Aaron said thank you for the seed, and Tomas clipped him round the head. {when: has(said.will_take_four)}
line: ANNI: Mum got down and went and stood in front of him. Right up close. She never said anything. He said order's the order. {when: has(said.will_take_six)}
line: ANNI: The inspector walked our Tomas down to the Captain. He shook his hand in the road. I saw him do it. {when: has(q.promised_hill)}
line: ANNI: They had the whole cart off us after, seed and all, and Mum never spoke to him again. {when: has(q.cart_stripped) | has(said.will_refuse_holt)}
line: ANNI: Your uncle Tomas got in the back of the Captain's car by himself. The step was too high for him. He had to use both hands. {when: q_cart == arrested}
line: DAUGHTER: Where did they take him? {when: q_cart == arrested}
line: ANNI: Up the hill. To Mrs Tesk's. {when: q_cart == arrested}
line: ANNI: That's what your gran said. I let her say it. {when: q_cart == arrested}
go: q.w.anni.next

@node q.w.anni.mary
place: q_anni_room
speaker: ANNI
cost: 2
line: ANNI: A lady came through in a trap with a rug on her knees. They lifted the pole for her without asking. She looked at me and told him I'd be fourteen. Like she was telling him something.
nar: The old man at the end of the table puts his cup down.
go: q.w.anni.next

@node q.w.anni.store
place: q_anni_room
speaker: ANNI
cost: 3
line: ANNI: The men at the Krall's End store said afterwards that somebody at the scale that morning let the Arlen man see how light it all was. In front of the whole queue. They didn't say it like it was a good thing. {when: q_figure == true}
line: ANNI: The men at the store said somebody at the scale pointed up the hill and said the Hesh had it under the goats. Everybody knows that, he said. They said it like it was clever. {when: q_figure == blamed}
line: ANNI: The men at the store said every cart weighed heavy on the square that winter, and the requisition came for what it weighed. Nobody said whose. {when: q_figure == inflated}
line: DAUGHTER: Who was it?
line: ANNI: A man in a coat.
go: q.w.anni.next

@node q.w.anni.granary
place: q_anni_room
speaker: ANNI
cost: 4
line: ANNI: That night the whole of Krall's End walked in to the granary. Mum had my wrist so I couldn't get to the front.
line: ANNI: Somebody inside dragged sacks up to the door and opened the little door in it, so we could see. They were ours. Mum knew her own patching. Then he told everybody what he'd seen. {when: q_door == talked, count: cost}
line: ANNI: They gave out a sack a family through the gap, and nobody said thank you. {when: q_door == talked}
line: ANNI: The door held. A soldier took somebody by the collar from the front and pulled him in. Mum said it was the Orme lad, by the coat. {when: q_door == held}
line: DAUGHTER: Was it? {when: q_door == held}
line: ANNI: The Orme lad had the fever in November. They buried him the week after. Everybody knew that. Mum knew it. {when: q_door == held}
line: ANNI: Mrs Orme was at the door. She heard a man inside tell the Captain how old he was. They kept him anyway. {when: q_door == held & has(said.ned_custody_age)}
line: ANNI: The door came in. There was a boy by a split sack with the grain running out round him. I didn't look to see who. {when: q_door == broken & !has(q.will_down)}
line: ANNI: The door came in on one of them. I went in with the lamp and held it over his face. I wanted to see which one he was. {when: has(q.will_down)}
line: ANNI: Mum saw one of them stood back by the sacks with a lantern. Just stood. She'd not let that go. {when: q_door == aside}
go: q.w.anni.next

@node q.w.anni.week
place: q_anni_room
speaker: ANNI
cost: 4
line: ANNI: On the Friday Dad went down to the office in his good cap, because they'd sent for him.
line: ANNI: On the Saturday, before it was light, he walked the soldiers up the path to Mrs Tesk's. In front of them. He knew the path in the dark. They brought her down. {when: has(q.ilo_mark)}
line: ANNI: Dad said one of them told him first, what they'd do to her. He went anyway. Tomas was downstairs. {when: has(said.ned_told_ilo) | has(said.will_told_ilo)}
line: ANNI: The doctor said intestinal. Your gran said he'd always had a weak stomach.
line: DAUGHTER: Had he?
line: ANNI: No.
go: q.w.anni.next

@node q.w.anni.yard
place: q_anni_room
speaker: ANNI
cost: 4
line: ANNI: On the Monday Gedge came to the yard. There was a goat chalked on our door.
line: ANNI: Dad went in and got Aaron's coat off the hook. He held it open for him, the way you do for a little one. Mum was at the window. {when: has(q.aaron_taken)}
line: ANNI: Somebody spoke up for us, and they went next door to Sallis's instead. I could hear them knocking. {when: !has(q.aaron_taken)}
line: ANNI: Mum saw a man at the top of the yard in a good coat. He stopped and watched, and then he went on to work. {when: has(said.ned_walked_on)}
go: q.w.anni.next

@node q.w.anni.gate
place: q_anni_room
speaker: ANNI
cost: 4
line: ANNI: I took the thread off myself at the door. Mum's fingers wouldn't do it. She held it in her mouth all the way home. {when: has(q.anni_sent)}
line: ANNI: He said something to the sister at the gate, about my father. Out loud. Nobody would tell me what he meant. {when: has(q.ned_claimed)}
line: ANNI: Mrs Furrowe opened the door and said wipe your feet. {when: has(q.anni_furrowe)}
line: ANNI: Somebody left bread on the step that week, wrapped in a man's handkerchief. Mum kept the handkerchief. {when: has(q.will_bread)}
line: ANNI: Mr Furrowe brought flour down in the trap. Dad didn't thank him. {when: has(q.ned_food)}
line: ANNI: Mum said no at the gate, and we went home. {when: !has(q.anni_sent) & !has(q.anni_furrowe)}
go: q.w.anni.next

@node q.w.anni.table
place: q_anni_room
speaker: ANNI
cost: 3
voice: knees: The arm says what it says. You only watch the arm. That's the whole of the job, and you've done it right for eleven years. {echo: q.sl.add_up, when: toldself(q.sl.add_up)}
voice: formletter: Nobody's going to climb up and look behind them. Nobody's going to come and check. {echo: q.sl.check, when: toldself(q.sl.check)}
line: ANNI: Mum laid the bowls every night after, all of them, and turned the empty ones over on the shelf. Every night. She wiped them. {when: has(q.tomas_held) | has(q.anni_sent) | has(q.aaron_taken) | has(q.anni_furrowe)}
line: ANNI: That week we were all at the table. All of us. I remember thinking that was a thing that could stop. {when: !(has(q.tomas_held) | has(q.anni_sent) | has(q.aaron_taken) | has(q.anni_furrowe))}
go: q.w.anni.next

@node q.w.anni.hands
place: q_anni_room
speaker: ANNI
cost: 3
nar: She looks at his hands on the cup.
line: ANNI: Edie Brack used to say her Davey never once let his own children see him cross. She said he sat on his hands at the table, like that.
voice: grip: You've never once lifted a hand to that boy. Not once. Your father did it every Friday and you swore. {echo: q.sl.never_hand, when: toldself(q.sl.never_hand)}
voice: precedent: Somebody had to keep order. You'll not hear different from me. {echo: q.sl.order, when: toldself(q.sl.order)}
go: q.w.anni.next

@node q.w.anni.guest
place: q_anni_room
speaker: ANNI
cost: 2
nar: She looks at him properly for the first time, the way she'd look at a sum. {when: has(said.ned_vouch_cart) | has(q.will_down) | has(q.ned_claimed)}
nar: The girl has the last length out of the tin. It's the only one with no knots in it at all, plain grey wool, gone soft with handling.
line: DAUGHTER: Why's this one got none?
line: ANNI: That's where my father goes.
line: DAUGHTER: So who was he?
line: ANNI: Ilo carried me on his shoulders to Osby fair, the year they bought the bowls.
line: DAUGHTER: That's not what I asked.
line: ANNI: No.
opt: "Say your name." -> q.w.anni.name {do: set(said.old_name)}
opt: "Put the knotted wool on the table." -> q.w.anni.tally ? has(said.ned_keep_tally)
opt: "Tell her where Tomas lies." -> q.w.anni.corner ? has(q.corner_known) | prior(q.fact.corner)
opt: "Say nothing." -> q.w.anni.quiet

@node q.w.anni.name
place: q_anni_room
speaker: ANNI
cost: 2
line: NED: Furrowe. With an e. {when: q_class == inspector}
line: ANNI: I know how it's spelt. {when: q_class == inspector}
line: WILL: Brack. Will Brack. I was at the post. {when: q_class == militia}
line: ANNI: I know where you were. {when: q_class == militia}
nar: She pours him more tea. He hadn't finished the first.
go: q.w.anni.next

@node q.w.anni.tally
place: q_anni_room
speaker: DAUGHTER
cost: 2
nar: He takes a coil of grey wool out of his inside pocket, soft with keeping, knotted all along, and puts it on the oilcloth. The knots have gone hard and dark with his hands. {sense: q.knots}
line: DAUGHTER: That's the one that's missing. Mum. That's October.
nar: Anni picks it up and puts it in the tin, in its place, in order. She doesn't say anything to him at all.
go: q.w.anni.next

@node q.w.anni.corner
place: q_anni_room
speaker: ANNI
cost: 3
nar: He tells her. He tells it badly, because he starts at the gap in the railings and has to go back, and because the corner is under the new section now, with wire round it and no markers.
line: ANNI: Was he awake?
nar: He wasn't there for that. He shakes his head.
line: ANNI: The corner past the gap. Where it's yellow.
nar: She nods. She'll go up on Sunday and stand at the wire, and nobody will know which bit to stand in front of, and she'll stand there anyway.
go: q.w.anni.next

@node q.w.anni.quiet
place: q_anni_room
cost: 2
nar: He says nothing. She doesn't ask him to. The rain goes on on the window.
go: q.w.anni.next

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the last beat: the effect that keeps moving
@node q.w.anni.tin
place: q_anni_room
speaker: DAUGHTER
cost: 3
do: wend()
line: DAUGHTER: Can I take the tin to school? Miss is doing the hard winter this term. She wants things from home.
line: ANNI: I'll think about it.
nar: The old man is still at the end of the table, with the cup in both hands, and it's gone cold. {when: has(said.old_name) | has(q.corner_known)}
nar: The chair at the end of the table is empty. The cup's still warm. {when: !(has(said.old_name) | has(q.corner_known))}
go: q.w.anni.next
